phases.title:
review UI + run history + retry panel + help. DONE SO FAR: useStickerTraceProgress (b8b45d62c) — live RTDB bar, stage-named label, nulls preserved. 🛑 MEASURED, and this phase is BIGGER than this note used to say: there are NO API routes at all (src/app/api/admin/sticker-sheets/** does not exist) and only TWO server actions — startStickerTraceRun and retryStickerTraceRun. There is no LIST action, so the run-history panel has nothing to call. So P9 is a ROUTE LAYER plus components:
  (1) a list action over stickerTraceRunsRepository.listBySheet, which already exists and is indexed (sheetId + createdAt desc was deployed in P4);
  (2) routes: upload sign/finalize, POST run (name REQUIRED — tester case 4), GET runs, POST retry, GET asset (signed URL), POST promote;
  (3) 🛑 audit-sticker-trace-egress must land WITH them — it scans those route files, so writing it first gives a zero-file rule that passes vacuously. Its property: no route under that tree may return a binary body; routes return JSON and binaries are 5-minute signed GCS URLs. This is the rule that protects against Root Cause #104, which PAUSED this project at 52.52 GB against a 10 GB allowance;
  (4) components: the commit flow through StickerTraceStudio's renderCommit slot, the run list, and the retry panel which must SHOW the clamp — explainResume() already returns the sentence;
  (5) the in-tool help panel (tiers, each advanced parameter, why a part was flagged).
🛑 Per-part thumbnails come from ONE sprite atlas plus geometry.json bboxes, never N image requests — object COUNT is metered separately from bytes.
